course: dictionary
lesson: 1984
title: Comprehend and comprehension
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: To comprehend something means to understand it fully, all the way through. In school, reading comprehension means understanding what you read, not just reading the words.
explain: «He could not comprehend how big the universe was.» He could read the words, but his mind could not yet take in how huge it is. Comprehend is the verb, and it shows the deep understanding you need.
explain: Formal exams often say «comprehend the question». This means understand what the question asks before you answer. Stop, read it again, and check what it wants.
fact: Comprehend is a verb: comprehend, comprehends, comprehended, comprehending.
fact: Comprehension is the noun: reading comprehension means understanding what you read.
fact: Comprehend can also mean to include or contain, but this is a formal meaning.
fact: Spelling rule: roots ending in d, de, se or nd usually take -sion, as in comprehend, comprehension.
fact: The same rule works for expand, expansion, and tense, tension.
exercise: «He could not comprehend how big the universe was.» What does comprehend mean here? | *To understand something fully | To sing very loudly | To fall asleep suddenly | To throw something far away
exercise: Which word is the noun for the understanding itself? | comprehended | comprehend | comprehending | *comprehension
exercise: Mia says, «I read the page twice but I could not comprehend it.» What does Mia mean? | She tore the page out | She understood it fully | She read it aloud to her friend | *She did not understand it
test: «After reading the story again, Sam finally ___ the ending.» Which word fits? | comprehension | comprehends the | *comprehended | compress
test: Using the spelling rule, which word is the -sion noun for tense? | tenser | tensed | *tension | tenses
exam: «The teacher asked us to comprehend the question before answering.» What does comprehend mean here? | To skip it and move on | To rub it out | To copy it onto the board | *To understand it fully
